.\" Manpage for worgenX
.TH WORGENX 1 "October 2026" "1.2.7" "worgenX Manual"
.SH NAME
worgenX \- Command line software for generating relevant wordlists, random passwords, and CPU benchmarking
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B worgenX
.RI < command > " [ options ]"
.SH DESCRIPTION
WorgenX is a powerful Rust wordlist generator with many functionalities :
.TP
- Generate a relevant wordlist with a custom mask and charset.
.TP
- Generate random passwords with customizable length and complexity with a strong entropy.
.TP
- Conduct CPU benchmarking to evaluate system performance.
.PP
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BR wordlist
Generate a wordlist
.TP
.BR password
Generate random password(s)
.TP
.BR benchmark
CPU Benchmark
.TP
.BR \-v, \-\-version
Display the version of WorgenX
.TP
.BR \-h, \-\-help
Display this help message
.SH "WORDLIST GENERATION OPTIONS"
.PP
You must specify at least one of the following options:
.TP
.BR \-l, \-\-lowercase
Add lowercase characters to the words
.TP
.BR \-u, \-\-uppercase
Add uppercase characters to the words
.TP
.BR \-n, \-\-numbers
Add numbers to the words
.TP
.BR \-x, \-\-special-characters
Add special characters to the words
.PP
These parameters are mandatory:
.TP
.BR \-m , \-\-mask " <mask>"
Mask used to generate the words
.TP
.BR \-o , \-\-output " <path>"
Save the wordlist in a text file
.PP
The following options are optional:
.TP
.BR \-d, \-\-disable-loading-bar
Disable the loading bar when generating the wordlist
.TP
.BR \-h, \-\-hash
Hash algorithm to use for the wordlist.
You can choose between: md5, sha1, sha224, sha256, sha384, sha512, sha3-224, sha3-256, sha3-384, sha3-512, blake2b, blake2s and whirlpool
.TP
.BR \-t , \-\-threads " <threads>"
Number of threads to generate the passwords. 
By default, the number of threads is based on the number of physical cores of the CPU
.SH "PASSWORD GENERATION OPTIONS"
.PP
You must specify at least one of the following options:
.TP
.BR \-l, \-\-lowercase
Add lowercase characters to the words
.TP
.BR \-u, \-\-uppercase
Add uppercase characters to the words
.TP
.BR \-n, \-\-numbers
Add numbers to the words
.TP
.BR \-x, \-\-special-characters
Add special characters to the words
.PP
These parameters are mandatory:
.TP
.BR \-s , \-\-size " <size>"
Size of the passwords in characters
.TP
.BR \-c , \-\-count " <count>"
Number of passwords to generate
.PP
The following options are optional:
.TP
.BR \-o , \-\-output " <path>"
Save the passwords in a file
.TP
.BR \-O , \-\-output-only " <path>"
Save the passwords only in a file, not in stdout
.TP
.BR \-j, \-\-json
Output in JSON format
Combine with -o to save the json output in a file
.SH "CPU BENCHMARK OPTIONS"
.PP
The following option is optional:
.TP
.BR \-t , \-\-threads " <threads>"
Number of threads to use for the CPU benchmark. 
By default, the number of threads is based on the number of physical cores of the CPU
.SH "SEE ALSO"
For more information, refer to the README file or visit the project page at https://github.com/XenorInspire/WorgenX.
